<title>USA: USDA SAYS IOWA FREE OF CATTLE DISEASE BRUCELLOSIS.</title>
<headline>USDA SAYS IOWA FREE OF CATTLE DISEASE BRUCELLOSIS.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Wednesday declared Iowa free of the cattle disease, brucellosis, relieving certain restrictions on interstate movement of the state's herds.</p>
<p>Brucellosis is a highly contagious cattle disease that causes animals to abort their calves and lower milk production. USDA has set a goal to eradicate the disease from the U.S. by the end of 1998. All but 12 states are now brucellosis free.</p>
</text>
